# Audit history is local product state, so it is not committed - except the five
# seeded runs, one per scenario. Those are tracked deliberately: without them a
# fresh clone opens the console on an empty page.
#
# The negations are not cosmetic. `railway up` builds its upload archive by
# respecting .gitignore, so an ignored file never reaches the build context and
# .dockerignore never gets a say. The deployed demo came up with zero runs until
# these lines existed.
evidence/runs/*.json
!evidence/runs/20260728T174522-89d397.json
!evidence/runs/20260728T175344-81df34.json
!evidence/runs/20260729T044318-0be937.json
!evidence/runs/20260729T050141-dc73ad.json
!evidence/runs/20260729T050250-693684.json
